## Context

Reading-3 (tracker [[0605]]). Two external Vietnam power-plant inventories
were surfaced for possible citation. Decision: cite one, log the other.

## A. Cite yuenhsu/Vietnam_Power_Plants in §2 + @misc

`https://github.com/yuenhsu/Vietnam_Power_Plants` — Yu En Hsu & Linh
Nguyen Phan Bao (Syracuse, Maxwell School; Ajello Fellowship; adv. Pete
Wilcoxen), 2020 snapshot. Merges WRI GPPD (pre-2016) + a 2018 market
report + **PDP7** (planned plants through 2030). It is the closest PRIOR
public compilation that also attempted the forward/planned tail — which is
this paper's distinctive contribution — so it clears the "cite
closely-related work" bar.

1. Add a `@misc` entry to `report/refs.bib` (key e.g.
   `Hsu-YuEn2020:vietnam-power-plants`): authors, year 2020, title,
   `howpublished = {GitHub repository}`, `url`, `urldate` (accessed
   2026-06-15). No DOI/license available — `@misc` is the right register
   (same as other data-repo citations).
2. One-clause mention in §2 "Open power-plant databases" paragraph
   (`sec:related-empirical`, ~`main.tex:178–200`, near the existing
   "closest external inventory" discussion): cite it as the closest
   PDP7-era prior compilation that reached for the planned tail, then
   distinguish ours: PDP8-era, per-cell provenance, coal+gas, maintained
   — vs its 2020/PDP7 snapshot, partly GPPD-derived, no per-cell sourcing,
   unmaintained. Lean the citation on the PDP7 planned-tail angle (the
   pre-2016 half is just GPPD, already cited).

## B. Seed the due-diligence note with the ODM coal dataset (NOT cited)

`https://data.vietnam.opendevelopmentmekong.net/.../thermal-coal-plants-in-vietnam-by-october-2020`
— Open Development Vietnam, Oct-2020 snapshot, CC BY-SA 4.0; coal-only;
statuses operational/under-construction/canceled/suspended. Sources:
"Vietnamese Wikipedia; Global Coal Plant Tracker; governmental reports and
media" — i.e. derivative of GEM GCPT (already cited `GEM2026:gcpt`) +
Wikipedia (already a recognition layer). NOT cited: adds no independent
coverage; coal-only; stale.

1. Add to the related-work due-diligence note (`docs/related-work/…` —
   the note [[0630]] also uses; create/extend it): entry "ODM thermal
   coal plants 2020 — surveyed, not cited: derivative of GCPT + Wikipedia,
   coal-only, 2020 snapshot."
2. Record the supporting observation: existing public Vietnam inventories
   are largely **derivative re-packs of GCPT and Wikipedia**, not
   independently sourced research-grade datasets — evidence for the
   paper's "first sourced / more comprehensive" framing. Optionally feed a
   one-clause version into §2 (no new citation needed for the observation).

